      "content": "The `userMemberSchema.parse(user)` call will throw a ZodError if the user object contains fields that are not defined in the schema. Since `removeSupplementaryFields` only removes fields based on the `select` query option, and the default behavior returns all fields, a member without `user:create` scope will receive a 500 error when the response includes admin-only fields (e.g., `isPending`, `isOwner`, `signInType`, `mfaEnabled`, `settings`, `personalizationAnswers`, `inviteAcceptUrl`, `lastActiveAt`, `projectRelations`). The schema should use `.strip()` or the controller should explicitly pick only the allowed fields before parsing. The integration test `should return limited fields for members without user:create scope` likely passes only because the test setup may not include those fields, but in production this will break."
